**[comments] Rule 4, comment lines that map to no code line: shorten**

The salt-range, token-position and 0x0800 sentences restate the constants N_SALT_RANGES_4, SALT_RANGE_0X4000, PATTERN_BASE_0X0800 and the expression on lines 371-372. 'NaN is unequal to itself. That would hide a correct copy.' maps to nothing here: every comparison goes through same_bits (lines 411, 443, 451, 471), which compares bits, so a NaN pattern would not hide a copy. The finiteness fact stays because it is why the base and range values were chosen (checked: the four salt ranges 0x0800..0x27ff, 0x4800..0x67ff, 0x8800..0xa7ff, 0xc800..0xe7ff avoid both inf/NaN ranges).

